[b00t]
name = "eureka-composite-capability"
type = "skill"
hint = "Eureka: capabilities built separately compose into obvious wins nobody planned — re-run the composition audit after every capability landing"
aliases = ["eureka", "eurkea"]

[b00t.schema]
type = "skill"
type_tags = ["eureka", "composition", "capability-audit", "assimilate", "grammar-verify", "serena", "meta-pattern"]

# ── The eureka (2026-07-07): capabilities compose behind your back ────────────
#
# Reviewing `b00t grok assimilate` against capabilities landed SINCE it was
# written exposed compositions that were invisible at authoring time and
# obvious in hindsight:
#
# 1. assimilate × grammar-verify:
#    concept_extractor.rs:43 BEGS the model — "Return ONLY valid JSON (no
#    markdown fences, no commentary)" — then degrades to empty extraction on
#    garbage. schema_constraint::constrain_request() (built days later) makes
#    malformed extraction UNREPRESENTABLE. The beg-and-degrade posture is
#    obsolete code the moment the constraint module landed; nobody noticed
#    because nobody re-audited the old surface against the new capability.
#
# 2. assimilate × serena (LSP symbolic ops):
#    assimilate ingests knowledge ABOUT tools; serena changes how agents READ
#    CODE (symbol-scoped, 83-96% measured token savings vs whole-file). The
#    hand-rolled cbm-code-discovery-gate hook was an ad-hoc attempt at exactly
#    this — a mature drop-in existed upstream the whole time.
#
# 3. z3-examples × datum emission:
#    S1-S5/A1-A3 were written as proofs; they ARE the audit half for any LLM
#    emitting b00t artifacts (S1 type-uniqueness audits assimilate output,
#    S3 acyclicity audits depends_on edges, A1 is pre-flight datum validation).
#
# 🤓 THE META-RULE: after every capability lands, walk the EXISTING surfaces
#    and ask "which of these was built as a workaround for not having this?"
#    Workarounds don't announce themselves — they look like normal code
#    (a begging prompt, a blocking hook, a proof nobody calls). The eureka
#    feels obvious precisely because the pieces already existed; the scarce
#    act is scheduling the re-audit, not having the insight.
#
# Recipe: b00t learn grammar-verify (constraint leg) · b00t learn serena
# (symbol leg) · cargo test -p b00t-c0re-lib --lib z3_ (audit leg).
# Candidate next compositions: distillery #98 × schema_constraint;
# sudo-operator disposition × schema_constraint; cbm hook → serena-backed gate.

# b00t:map v1
# summary: Composition audit meta-pattern — re-walk existing surfaces after each capability lands; workarounds look like normal code
